hadiths[46]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abu 'Amr ash-Shaybani said, \The owner of this house (and he pointed at\nthe house of 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud) said"
"2","Muhammad ibn Sirin related that Abu Hurayra blew his nose in his\ngarment and then said, \Squirt! Squirt! Abu Hurayra blows his nose\nin linen. You saw me lying between 'A'isha's room and the minbar\nwhen people said I was crazy"
"3","Bahz ibn Hakim's grandfather said, \I asked"
"4","Shahr ibn Hawshab said, \Me and my maternal aunt visited 'A'isha\nand said"
"5","Abu Hurayra said, \The Prophet was asked"
"6","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \Beware of suspicion. Suspicion is the worst type of lie. Do not spy. Do not fight one another. Do not try\nto ensnare one another (in sales). Do not envy each other. Do not hate one another. Be slaves of\nAllah and brothers.\"""""
"7","He told us, he said: He told us, he said: He said: There is no Muslim whose parents are both Muslims who does not have a good end, except that Allah will open for him two doors, meaning the gates of Paradise, whether one or both. And if one of them is angry with him, Allah will not be pleased with him until he is pleased with him. It was said: What if they punish him? He said: What if they punish him."
"8","'Abdullah said, \The person who has had something stolen from\nhim continues to be suspicious until he is worse than the thief.\"""""
"9","Bilal ibn Sa'd al-Ash'ari related that Mu'awiya wrote to Abu Dharr,\n\Write down for me the deviants of Damascus.\"" Abu Dharr said"
"10","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \A child cannot repay his father unless he finds him as\na slave and the buys him and sets him free.\"""""
"11","circumcision, shaving\nthe pubic hair, plucking the armpits, clipping the moustache and clipping\nthe nails.\""12"""
"12","Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Murrah, the freed slave of Aqil, that Abu Hurayrah was appointed as deputy by Marwan, and he was at Dhu al-Hulayfah. His mother was in one house and he was in another. He said: When he wanted to go out, he would stand at her door and say: ""Peace be upon you, O my mother, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings."" She would say: ""And upon you be peace, O my son, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings."" He would say: ""May Allah have mercy on you as you raised me when I was small."" She would say: ""May Allah have mercy on you as you treated me dutifully when I was old."" Then when he wanted to enter, he would do the same."
"13","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance for hijrah (migration), while he had left his parents weeping. He said: ""Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."""
"14","Abd al-Rahman bin Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Fudayk informed me, saying: Musa informed me, from Abu Hazim, that Abu Murra, the freed slave of Umm Hanee', daughter of Abu Talib, informed him, saying: Abu Hurayrah and I rode together to his land in al-'Aqi. When I entered his land, he called out at the top of his voice: ""Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings, O family of yours."" They would say: ""And peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings."" He would say: ""May Allah have mercy on you. He raised me as a young boy."" They would say: ""O son, and you were raised by Allah, and He will recompense you with good and be pleased with you, just as He raised you as an old man."" Musa said: The name of Abu Hurayrah was Abd Allah bin Amr."
"15","Al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba reported that a man said, \May Allah make\nthe amir thrive! Your chamberlain recognises certain men and gives them\npreference in permission to enter.\"" He said"
"16","Ibrahim said, \Our companions used to allow us all sorts of play\nthings except for dogs.\"""""
"17","Abu 'Uqba said, \I once walked along the road with Ibn 'Umar.\nI passed some Abyssinian lads who were playing and he brought out two dirhams\nwhich he gave to them.\"""""
"18","'A'isha reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, used to call her companions to her who were playing with dolls.\""19"""
"19","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""I have come to pledge allegiance to you for hijrah, and I left my parents weeping."" He said: ""Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."""
"20","Al-Hasan said, \'Uthman did not speak on any Jumu'a without commanding\nthe killing of dogs and slaughtering of doves.\"""""
"21","Zayd ibn Thabit reported that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab came to him\nto ask to see him one day and he gave him permission while his head was\nin the hands of a slavegirl of his who was combing his hair. He removed\nhis head and 'Umar said to him, 'Let her comb it.' He said, 'Amir al-Mu'minin,\nif you were to send for me, I would come to you.' ''Umar said, 'It is my\nneed.'\""22"""
"22","Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Zabban ibn Fai'd, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever is dutiful to his parents, glad tidings for him; Allah Mighty and Majestic increases his lifespan."""
"23","Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Husayn narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, in the saying of Allah the Exalted: ""Either one of them reaches old age with you, or both of them, so do not say to them 'Uff'."" Until the verse was abrogated in the following: ""What Allah's Messenger and those who believed with him did not ask forgiveness from the polytheists, even though they were their closest relatives, after it became clear to them that they were the companions of the Fire."""
"24","Abu Mulayka related that when it rained, Ibn 'Abbas said, \Slavegirl!\nBring out my saddle and bring my garment. Allah says"
"25","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, commanded that whips be hung up in houses."
"26","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \Beware of conversing after the night\nis still. None of you knows what creatures Allah will send"
"27","Jabir reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \Keep children in until the evening has completely fallen.\nThat time is the hour when the shaytans come out.\"""""
"28","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr said, \A man's reviling his father is one of the major\nwrong actions in the sight of Allah Almighty.\"""""
"29","Abu Bakra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, said, \There is no wrong action more likely to bring punishment in\nthis world in addition to what is stored up in the Next World than oppression\nand severing ties of kinship.\"""""
"30","What you say about fornication, drinking wine, and theft? We said: ""God and His Messenger know best."" He said: ""Those are the shameful acts, and in them are the punishments. Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the great sins? Associating with Allah, and being disobedient to one's parents, and being a spendthrift?"""
"31","Ibn 'Umar said, \Making parents weep is part of disobedience and one\nof the major wrong actions.\"""""
"32","the\nsupplication of someone who is oppressed, the supplication of someone on\na journey, and the supplication of parents for their children.\""33"""
"33","Ayyash ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Shurahbil, the brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""No infant spoke in the cradle except Jesus son of Mary ﷺ, and the companion of Jurayj."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, and who is the companion of Jurayj?"" He said: ""Jurayj was a man, a monk in his hermitage. There was a cowherd who would take shelter at the bottom of his hermitage. A woman from the village would visit the cowherd. One day his mother came and said: 'O Jurayj,' while he was praying. He said to himself while praying: 'My mother or my prayer?' He chose to prefer his prayer. Then she called him a second time, and he said to himself: 'My mother or my prayer?' He chose to prefer his prayer. Then she called him a third time, and he said: 'My mother or my prayer?' He chose to prefer his prayer. When he did not answer her, she said: 'May Allah not let you die, O Jurayj, until you look at the faces of the prostitutes.' Then she left. Then that woman was brought to the king after she had given birth. He said: 'From whom?' She said: 'From Jurayj.' He said: 'The owner of the hermitage?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Demolish his hermitage and bring him to me.' So they struck his hermitage with axes until it collapsed. They put a rope around his neck and led him away. He passed by the prostitutes, saw them, and smiled, while they looked at him among the people. The king said: 'What does this woman claim?' He said: 'What does she claim?' He said: 'She claims that her child is from you.' He said: 'You claim that?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Where is this child?' They said: 'He is in her lap.' He turned to him and said: 'Who is your father?' He said: 'The cowherd.' The king said: 'Shall we make your hermitage of gold?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Of silver?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then what shall we make it?' He said: 'Return it as it was.' He said: 'What made you smile?' He said: 'A matter I recognized; my mother's supplication reached me.' Then he informed them."""
"34","Abu Hurayra said, \Neither Jew nor Christian has heard me and then not\nloved me. I wanted my mother to become Muslim"
"35","Supplication for them, asking\nforgiveness for them, fulfilling their pledges, and being generous to friends\nof theirs. You only have ties of kinship through your parents.\""36"""
"36","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The deceased's rank is raised after his death. He says: ""O my Lord, what is this?"" It is said: ""Your child sought forgiveness for you."""
"37","Ibn Sirin said, \We were with Abu Hurayra one night and he said"
"38","sadaqa which continues, knowledge\nwhich benefits, or a righteous child who makes supplication for him.\""39"""
"39","Yasarah ibn Safwan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, my mother died without making a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?"" He said: ""Yes."""
"40","'Abdullah ibn Dinar reported that Ibn 'Umar passed by a bedouin during\na journey. The bedouin's father had been a friend of 'Umar's. The bedouin\nsaid, \Am I not the son of so-and-so?\"" He said"
"41","Ibn 'Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \The strongest form of dutifulness is when a man maintains\nrelations with the people his father loved.\"""""
"42","Sa'd ibn 'Ubada az-Zurqi reported that his father said, \I was sitting\nin the mosque in Madina with 'Amr ibn 'Uthman when 'Abdullah ibn Salam walked\nby"
"43","Abu Bakr ibn Hazm reported that one of the Companions of the Prophet,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \It is enough that I tell\nyou that the Messenger of Allah"
"44","Abu Hurayra saw two men and said to one of them, \Who is this man in\nrelation to you?\"" He is my father"
"45","Shahr ibn Hawshab said, \We went out with Ibn 'Umar and Salim said to\nhim"
"46","'Abdullah ibn Dinar said reported that Ibn 'Umar said, \But Abu Hafs\n'Umar decided...\"""""
